en by malware for exfiltration.\nAn adversary might compress data (e.g., sensitive documents) that is collected prior to exfiltration in order to make it portable and minimize the amount of data sent over the network.\n", "rule_author": "Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113", "match_context": [{"values": {"CommandLine": "powershell -NonInteractive -WindowStyle Hidden -Command \"Compress-Archive -Path 'C:\\Users\\OQXZRA~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\DE-10.10.2026\\*' -DestinationPath 'C:\\Users\\OQXZRA~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\DE-10.10.2026.zip' -Force\"", "Image": "powershell", "EventID": "1"}}]}, {"rule_level": "low", "rule_id": "0f8e3c8e1fbbfbe7cf4a673a7445d726cd5c91d52f036a090b8e242dd368058e", "rule_source": "Sigma Integrated Rule Set (GitHub)", "rule_title": "Suspicious File Access to Browser Credential Storage", "rule_description": "Detects file access to browser credential storage paths by non-browser processes, which may indicate credential access attempts.\nAdversaries may attempt to access browser credential storage to extract sensitive information such as usernames and passwords or cookies.\nThis behavior is often commonly observed in credential stealing malware.\n", "rule_author": "frack113, X__Junior (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems), Parth-FourCore", "match_context": [{"values": {"FileName": "c:\\users\\oqxzraykm\\appdata\\local\\microsoft\\edge\\user data\\default\\network\\cookies"}}, {"values": {"FileName": "c:\\users\\oqxzraykm\\appdata\\local\\microsoft\\edge\\user data\\default\\login data"}}]}], "times_submitted": 1}}}